2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  CLAIM    T0153 the recorder's resampler was built with in_rate == out_rate == settings.audio.sampleRate, so a 44.1 kHz sink was labelled 48 kHz (plays ~8.8 % fast) and no rate conversion ever happened
2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  CHANGE   src/recorder/VideoRecorderThread.cpp:163 passes AudioQueue::sampleRate() into encodeAudio. That is the sink-observed rate, and the only place it is known.
2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  CHANGE   src/recorder/VideoRecorderFFmpeg.cpp: encodeAudio rebuilds swrCtx_ when a batch's rate/channel count disagrees with the side it was built for (swrInRate_/swrInChannels_, cleared by cleanup, so a new take never inherits the last one's time base). configureResampler is the one place a context is built.
2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  CHANGE   The rate alone was not enough, which is the part that looked fixed and was not: the old loop converted one encoder frame at a time and then erased a fixed frameSize * channels of input per frame, whether or not swr had consumed it. A correct in_rate still shed ~8 % of every 4096-frame batch. encodeAudio now converts the whole batch into a scratch frame in the encoder's format (sized from swr_get_out_samples, the documented bound) and cuts whole frames out of a per-plane FIFO, so nothing is discarded for being early.
2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  NEGATIVE swr_get_delay is not a shortcut for "how much input do I need for one fixed-size output frame": fed back into the input sizing it diverged, measured delay 17 -> 35 -> 70 -> 141 -> 283 -> 566 output samples, because each call supplied more input than the fixed output room could drain and swr buffered the surplus. The batch-convert-then-cut design needs no delay arithmetic at all.
2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  CHANGE   src/recorder/VideoRecorderFFmpeg.{hpp,cpp}: resampleIntoAudioFrame is a pure convert now; ensureResampleScratch/appendPending own the scratch frame and the FIFO; encodedAudioSamplesForTesting() exposes the sample count. The simulateResampleFailureForTesting seam is charged per frame where the frame is formed, not per convert (one convert is several frames at a rate ratio), mirroring consumeInjectedWriteFailure.
2026-10-22T09:40:00Z  CHANGE   src/recorder/ResamplerEngine.hpp and TODO.md T0153 text: the doc no longer claims the recorder does no rate conversion.
